1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:08,807
Priya Patel changed her mind: the vanity is now natural oak, not white. Change the whole job’s materials at once.

2
00:00:08,807 --> 00:00:12,168
Before: everything is white melamine. Note the sheet list.

3
00:00:12,168 --> 00:00:18,320
Cabinets tab → Change materials. Each picker shows what the job uses now.

4
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:27,260
Carcass and fronts: PB18-OAK, the natural oak melamine with grain.

5
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:36,413
The edgebanding follows: oak ABS on the carcass front edges and on the doors and drawer fronts.

6
00:00:36,413 --> 00:00:41,874
Drawer boxes stay at "Keep as is": 16 mm white, the side thickness TANDEM slides are made for.

7
00:00:41,874 --> 00:00:54,708
Preview: every part that changes, sheets before and after, and no new warnings.

8
00:00:54,708 --> 00:00:59,278
Apply to both cabinets. (One Undo would put it all back.)

9
00:00:59,278 --> 00:01:11,969
The cut list regroups by material: oak parts, the white drawer boxes and the backs.

10
00:01:11,969 --> 00:01:16,896
The edgeband totals switch to the oak tape.

11
00:01:16,896 --> 00:01:24,592
Nesting re-runs on its own: oak sheets now, with the grain kept along each part.

12
00:01:24,592 --> 00:01:28,334
A change of finish on a whole job takes one dialog, and the cut list, nesting and labels all follow.
